{
  "version": 1,
  "comment": "The model catalog (design section 6): data, not code. 'profiles' maps each profile to a default model id per provider kind; routing.profiles in settings overrides it. 'families' lists capability descriptors for known model families, matched in order against the model id (case-insensitive, '*' is a wildcard); the last entry must be the '*' default. Providers that report capabilities themselves (Ollama's /api/show) override the chat, fim, vision, tools and embeddings flags and the context window; the OpenAI-compatible adapter reads only the context window, when /models reports one. The openai and openai-compatible defaults are OpenAI model ids taken from the OpenAI model list in October 2026 and are only defaults: set routing.profiles (bare id or provider/model) for a gateway with different ids, such as OpenRouter's openai/... names. The context windows of the gpt-6 family are conservative placeholders. Costs are left at 0 (unknown) until the cost governor ships.",
